v 3
d synthgen. Generate a rank-preserving synthetic stand-in dataset.
d
d synthgen builds a synthetic dataset that behaves like the source
d without containing any of its records: each variable's observed
d distribution is reproduced exactly (every synthetic value is an
d observed value), the rank (Spearman) correlations between
d variables are preserved through a Gaussian-copula draw, and each
d variable's missing share is re-imposed.  Refuses string and
d ID-shaped variables loudly, with no override.  Every run returns
d a utility-and-safety receipt: worst standardized mean gap, worst
d rank-correlation gap, and the count of synthetic rows duplicating
d a real record.
d
d Requires: Stata 16+.  No Python or other external dependencies.
d
d KW: synthetic data
d KW: privacy
d KW: disclosure
d KW: copula
d KW: data sharing
d
d Authors: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
